## P18-V01 rebalance continuation

- Corrected Push assignment-source selection to use the pinned
  `RebalancePushImpl.clientRebalance(topic)`. The `isOrder` argument no longer
  selects local versus Broker assignment; LiteSelective follows the same
  pinned distinction.
- Restored pinned clustering route handling: a missing or empty route is
  handled before membership lookup, leaves active assignments and the current
  balance result intact, and notifies empty sets for non-retry topics.
  Broadcasting with a missing route also notifies empty sets without marking
  the pass unbalanced.
- New Push `ProcessQueue` assignments now start with `locked=true`; the
  initialization timestamp is captured before offset lookup, matching the
  pinned create/setLocked/compute-offset order. A Broker lock request is sent
  only for `isOrder` assignments outside the broadcasting branch.
- Focused regressions cover missing/empty clustering routes, missing
  broadcasting routes, client-rebalance source selection, LiteSelective Broker
  selection, and the initial ProcessQueue lock flag.
- Final verification on this change: `cargo test -p
  rocketmq-classic-consumer --lib` (241 passed), strict consumer Clippy with all
  targets/features and `-D warnings`, `cargo fmt --check`, and `git diff
  --check` all pass. An earlier Clippy run exposed a test mutex-guard scope;
  the test was corrected and the final lint run passed.

